---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const images = [
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/01-if-i-go-you-re-going-with-me.png",
    "title": "If I Go, You're Going With Me",
    "caption": "Epic wide shot: inside a smooth alien mountain bore, a gaunt mind flayer slumps on a crystal-and-gear laser throne, robes shredded, as furry white yeti-like quaggoths claw at him. With his last strength he slams a glowing lever."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/02-the-poke-in-the-butt.png",
    "title": "The Poke in the Butt",
    "caption": "Comic-heroic action shot: a tiny Kobold paladin riding a winged flying elephant lunges with a glowing rapier straight into the hindquarters of a colossal dragon whose head is a pulsing exposed elder brain with face tentacles. The dragon's eyes go wide in outrage."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/03-up-the-spine.png",
    "title": "Up the Spine",
    "caption": "Low-angle, dramatic: a battered Dragonborn fighter, barely alive, sprints up the scaled spine of a fallen brain-dragon hybrid and drives his rapier down its back, slicing as he slides. Glistening illithid tadpoles spill from the wound."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/04-bring-the-wrath.png",
    "title": "Bring the Wrath",
    "caption": "A massive Goliath barbarian in full rage, mouth open in a bloodcurdling scream of giant-tongue curses, gouges a glaive deep into the flank of a gargantuan dragon-elder brain hybrid. A face tentacle lashes at him and misses."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/05-life-is-pain.png",
    "title": "Life Is Pain",
    "caption": "Close-up, mournful: a dying mind flayer on a crystal throne, torn apart by shaggy quaggoth claws, tentacles drooping, sends one last psychic message, shown as a faint violet ripple spreading outward into the dark. His expression is resigned, almost serene."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/06-maximally-lava-y.png",
    "title": "Maximally Lava-y",
    "caption": "Wide shot: a vast cavern pit collapsing as dynamite blasts rip through its rim. Rocks tumble, and stunned mind flayers are swept down into rivers of glowing lava below."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/07-out-through-the-tear.png",
    "title": "Out Through the Tear",
    "caption": "A raw, flesh-edged rip in reality hangs in the air of a gray irradiated wasteland. Through it, a blinding white frozen ice sheet and polar sky are visible."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-118/08-clever-things.png",
    "title": "Clever Things",
    "caption": "In a candlelit gothic library in Ludendorff, a tall, lanky, angular Warforged with dulled lacquer, faded heraldry and a registration mark on his forehead (K-2SO proportions) leans over a jar holding a mind flayer's brain with cold curiosity. A tiny mechanical hummingbird homunculus has just snatched the jar from a startled Kobold paladin's hands."
  }
]
---

<Layout title="Session 118 — Tales of the Radiant Citadel" description="The party killed the High Master, the Elder Brain Dragon. Erik's notes call it the closest the party has come to a wipe in the whole campaign. QDV, already">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <a href="/studio" class="text-sm text-earth hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">&larr; Studio</a>

    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black leading-tight mb-2">
      Session 118
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-earth mb-1">Tales of the Radiant Citadel &middot; October 20, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mb-8">Bluetspur Expedition (Finale, Part 2) → return to Lamordia</p>

    <div class="prose-section text-ink-light leading-relaxed mb-12 space-y-4">
      <p>
        The party killed the High Master, the Elder Brain Dragon. Erik's notes call it the closest the party has come to a wipe in the whole campaign. QDV, already mauled by quaggoths, fired one last orbital strike at the dragon knowing it would cost him his life. Gemnar and Haru landed crits, and Kiet, back up on 1 HP, ran up the dragon's spine and slashed it open. The party buried the remaining mind flayers in lava. Instead of using a teleport spell, they went home through the tear Kiet had cut in reality, landing on Lamordia's ice sheet with QDV's skull and brain in tow. In Ludendorff, the mutations were cleared and <strong>Gordian</strong> made his debut in the library.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Highlights</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-12 list-disc list-inside">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Tadpole Breath</strong> — Sam, to Kiet: <em>&quot;And that is certainly a number that you have rolled. Great. The bad news is you are infested with tadpoles. Don't worry about all the text of that. The 59 damage is the part that matters right now.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Moonbeam on a Dead World</strong> — Toven upcasts Moonbeam to 5th level. Sam: <em>&quot;It's like a sunbeam, but reflective, but colder... The cracked and withered moon over this land shines down and casts a beam onto this guy.&quot;</em> Erik: <em>&quot;Got orbital lasers.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Mind Flayers and Hulks</strong> — The party's three Star Spawn Hulk allies are the flayers' first targets. One Hulk is dominated at once: <em>&quot;Your friend is now his friend. That happened quickly and easily.&quot;</em> Two others take 27 from a Mind Blast and are stunned.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Quaggoths Find QDV</strong> — The furry ex-slaves reach QDV's laser throne: <em>&quot;Boink, boink. Boink.&quot;</em> He takes 71 slashing; his psychic immunity blocks the rest. Erik: <em>&quot;I'm getting hit by some Quaggoth thoughts.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Gemnar Goes Berserk</strong> — Reckless Attack, a crit on the first swing, a second hit, and a bonus-action attack from the crit. Sam: <em>&quot;You do in one attack more damage than Kiat did in an entire 2 turns of attacks. Sorry, Kiat.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">QDV's Last Orbital Strike</strong> — Erik: <em>&quot;My only question is whether I target myself, to free me from this horrible attack, or if I target the dragon.&quot;</em> He picks the dragon: <em>&quot;He's gonna focus all his rage on the one who started this... If I go, you're going with me.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Poke in the Butt</strong> — Stomper dashes in, and Haru spends a bonus action on Lay on Hands: 1 HP to Kiet. <em>&quot;It's amazing what 1 HP can do in this world.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kiet Kills the High Master</strong> — Jonas: <em>&quot;Coming in from the back and just like stabbing in the middle of the back and just like slashing down.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">QDV Dies</strong> — The quaggoths come back to finish tearing him apart: <em>&quot;Does 39 damage tear you to shreds?&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Mop-Up: Lava and Dynamite</strong> — Kiet keeps fighting on 1 HP. Erik: <em>&quot;With 1 HP, you're just going Jet Li on this guy. I love it.&quot;</em> Sam hints that a trip over a crack sends a flayer into the lava. Kiet knocks <strong>two</strong> of them in.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Spoils and Credit</strong> — Gemnar takes a tentacle (for a belt), a claw, and <em>&quot;the dimming eye out of this monstrosity.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Home Through the Tear</strong> — There's a teleport spell ready, but Kiet pushes for the reality tear from his <em>&quot;skunkworks infinity knife.&quot;</em> Table objection: <em>&quot;Doesn't that damage the whole fabric of the universe?&quot;</em> / <em>&quot;Let's do it. Let's save the spell.&quot;</em></li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Ludendorff, Changed</strong> — Greater Restoration clears every mutation: <em>&quot;Bit by bit, you shrink heads back down to size. You put Kiet's legs back on.&quot;</em> Everyone is back to their original character sheet.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Gordian</strong> — Sam sets the scene in the Ludendorff library: <em>&quot;I think that's a better intro perhaps for who your character is.&quot;</em></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Art</h2>
    <div class="space-y-10">
      {images.map((img) => (
        <figure>
          <img
            src={img.src}
            alt={img.title}
            class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">{img.title}</span>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mt-1">{img.caption}</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-cream-dark mt-16 pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold mb-3">Party</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">QDV → Gordian</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Erik)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Kiet</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Jonas)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Virgil Gemnar</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Kyle)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Toven</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Max)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Haru</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Hunter)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">DM</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Sam)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
